{
  "_comment": [
    "Static dealer data. The save keeps a dealer's Id and how its business is going (open, closing down,",
    "closed, waiting to open), so this file is the truth for the rest and is merged over the saved dealers on",
    "load. Adding a field here reaches every existing save.",
    "",
    "mapX/mapY are fractions of the WHOLE map picture (map.json: los_angeles_map.jpg, the Automobile Club of",
    "Southern California road map, 2444 x 1560), measured from its top left. The screen shows a crop of it; the",
    "crop is map.json's anchor, so moving the crop does not mean moving every pin. Replacing the map picture",
    "DOES mean re-reading every pin off it, because these are fractions of that picture.",
    "",
    "travelHours is the round trip from the garage and is meant to match the map: the lots round downtown",
    "are an hour, the valley and the harbour two, and Riverside is most of a morning.",
    "",
    "priceBandLow/High is the dealer's slice of the market, measured as the share of installed cars it is",
    "dearer than - not as dollars, so it means the same thing whatever is installed. The bands overlap on",
    "purpose; where they do, chance decides. Between them they must cover 0 to 1 or some cars have nowhere",
    "to go.",
    "",
    "stockLow/High is how many cars the lot carries. Keep it at or under the capacity of its showroom in",
    "showrooms.json, or the overflow can only be read about and never seen. Bays are worked out from the",
    "room and the number of cars, so there is nothing to author here.",
    "",
    "startsOpen false: the dealer is not in business when a game starts, and opens some day when the market has",
    "room for another lot (DealerLifeService). About 60% of the dealers are open at a time; now and then one goes",
    "out of business and one of these opens. A save made before a dealer existed gets it the same way."
  ],
